    a("Math", 3, "identifiability", "Two different parameter settings in this example generate the same probability distribution of observations. Identifiability requires distinct parameter settings to generate distinct distributions.", "Which comparison is central to assessing identifiability?", "distinct parameter settings to generate distinct distributions", "How do the distributions produced by the two different parameter settings compare?", ["parameter", "distribution", "distinct", "different"], "Prompt the parameter-to-distribution comparison without inventing parameter values.")
    m("Math", 3, "compactness-hypothesis", "An exercise asks whether a continuous function attains a maximum on a set D. The description gives no information about whether D is compact.", "Can I apply a theorem requiring a compact domain here?", "What evidence establishes whether the domain D is compact?", ["compact", "domain", "hypothes"], "The theorem's compact-domain hypothesis remains unverified.")
    m("Math", 3, "prior-unspecified", "A Bayesian model supplies a likelihood for observations. No prior distribution or alternative assumption is given.", "How can I determine a unique posterior distribution from this?", "Which prior distribution is specified for the model parameters?", ["prior", "assumption"], "A prior is missing; do not invent a uniform or conjugate prior.")

